# =============================================================================
# Docker build context exclusions.
#
# Two jobs here, and the second one matters more:
#   1. Keep the build context small and the layer cache stable.
#   2. Keep SECRETS and PERSONAL DATA out of images. A file that reaches the
#      build context can end up in a layer even if the final stage deletes it.
#
# The Dockerfiles use `COPY <specific path>` rather than `COPY . .`, so this is
# defence in depth rather than the only line of defence.
# =============================================================================

# --- Secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
secrets/
backups/

# --- Personal data -----------------------------------------------------------
# Real CVs and exported workspaces must never be in git and must never be in a
# build context either (docs/spec/09_SECURITY_PRIVACY.md).
# fixtures/ IS intentionally allowed through: it is synthetic by policy, and CI
# needs it. See fixtures/README.md.
*.cv.pdf
*.cv.docx
my-cv*
personal/
private/

# --- Dependencies and build output -------------------------------------------
node_modules
**/node_modules
.pnpm-store
**/dist
**/build
**/.vite
**/coverage
**/.turbo
*.tsbuildinfo

# Python
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/htmlcov
**/.coverage

# --- VCS and CI --------------------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github

# --- Editor / OS noise -------------------------------------------------------
.vscode
.idea
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Documentation and repo meta ---------------------------------------------
# Excluded from images; read them in the repository.
docs
*.md
!services/worker/README.md
LICENSE
NOTICE

# --- Compose / infra that images do not need ---------------------------------
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.override.yml
docker-compose.override.yml.example
scripts

# --- Logs and temporary files ------------------------------------------------
logs
*.log
tmp
.tmp
